ah, the son of Hezekiah, in the days of Josiah, the son of Amon, king of Judah."},{"verse":2,"text":"I will utterly sweep away everything from the surface of the earth, says the LORD."},{"verse":3,"text":"I will sweep away man and animal. I will sweep away the birds of the sky, the fish of the sea, and the heaps of rubble with the wicked. I will cut off man from the surface of the earth, says the LORD."},{"verse":4,"text":"I will stretch out my hand against Judah and against all the inhabitants of Jerusalem. I will cut off the remnant of Baal from this place—the name of the idolatrous and pagan priests,"},{"verse":5,"text":"those who worship the army of the sky on the housetops, those who worship and swear by the LORD and also swear by Malcam,"},{"verse":6,"text":"those who have turned back from following the LORD, and those who haven’t sought the LORD nor inquired after him."},{"verse":7,"text":"Be silent at the presence of the Lord GOD, for the day of the LORD is at hand. For the LORD has prepared a sacrifice. He has consecrated his guests."},{"verse":8,"text":"It will happen in the day of the LORD’s sacrifice that I will punish the princes, the king’s sons, and all those who are clothed with foreign clothing."},{"verse":9,"text":"In that day, I will punish all those who leap over the threshold, who fill their master’s house with violence and deceit."},{"verse":10,"text":"In that day, says the LORD, there will be the noise of a cry from the fish gate, a wailing from the second quarter, and a great crashing from the hills."},{"verse":11,"text":"Wail, you inhabitants of Maktesh, for all the people of Canaan are undone! All those who were loaded with silver are cut off."},{"verse":12,"text":"It will happen at that time, that I will search Jerusalem with lamps, and I will punish the men who are settled on their dregs, who say in their heart, “The LORD will not do good, neither will he do evil.”"},{"verse":13,"text":"Their wealth will become a plunder, and their houses a desolation. Yes, they will build houses, but won’t inhabit them. They will plant vineyards, but won’t drink their wine."},{"verse":14,"text":"The great day of the LORD is near. It is near and hurries greatly, the voice of the day of the LORD. The mighty man cries there bitterly."},{"verse":15,"text":"That day is a day of wrath, a day of distress and anguish, a day of trouble and ruin, a day of darkness and gloom, a day of clouds and blackness,"},{"verse":16,"text":"a day of the trumpet and alarm against the fortified cities and against the high battlements."},{"verse":17,"text":"I will bring such distress on men that they will walk like blind men because they have sinned against the LORD. Their blood will be poured out like dust and their flesh like dung."},{"verse":18,"text":"Neither their silver nor their gold will be able to deliver them in the day of the LORD’s wrath, but the whole land will be devoured by the fire of his jealousy; for he will make an end, yes, a terrible end, of all those who dwell in the land."}],"hasArtwork":true,"artworkUrl":"/data/images/books/zephaniah.svg","availableLangs":["zh-CN"]},{"id":"zephaniah_2","bookSlug":"zephaniah","chapter":2,"reference":"Zephaniah 2","title":"Zephaniah 2 — Public Domain Study","topics":["zephaniah","zephaniah","ot","scripture","西番雅書","西番雅书","呼籲百姓悔改","呼吁百姓悔改"],"snippet":{"zh-CN":"不知羞耻的国民哪，你们应当聚集！ 趁命令没有发出， 日子过去如风前的糠， 耶和华的烈怒未临到你们， 他发怒的日子未到以先， 你们应当聚集前来。"},"tokens":{"15":2,"36":1,"zephaniah":9,"public":2,"domain":2,"study":1,"ot":1,"scripture":1,"西番雅書":1,"西番雅书":2,"呼籲百姓悔改":1,"呼吁百姓悔改":1,"不知羞耻的国民哪":1,"你们应当聚集":1,"趁命令没有发出":1,"日子过去如风前的糠":1,"耶和华的烈怒未临到你们":1,"他发怒的日子未到以先":1,"你们应当聚集前来":1,"世上遵守耶和华典章的谦卑人哪":1,"你们都当寻求耶和华":1,"当寻求公义谦卑":1,"或者在耶和华发怒的日子可以隐藏起来":1,"迦萨必致见弃":1,"亚实基伦必然荒凉":1,"人在正午必赶出亚实突的民":1,"以革伦也被拔出根来":1,"住沿海之地的基利提族有祸了":1,"迦南":2,"非利士人之地啊":1,"耶和华的话与你反对":1,"我必毁灭你":1,"以致无人居住":1,"沿海之地要变为草场":1,"其上有牧人的住处和羊群的圈":1,"这地必为犹大家剩下的人所得":1,"他们必在那里牧放群羊":1,"晚上必躺卧在亚实基伦的房屋中":1,"因为耶和华":1,"他们的":1,"神必眷顾他们":1,"使他们被掳的人归回":1,"我听见摩押人的毁谤和亚扪人的辱骂":